 "notes": "Single map sheet read from OCR (page 1). Map symbols beside unit names are garbled or blank ('[ oxtw |', '7]', '[™ ]', '[ 1 |') and were not recorded. The Water unit was not recorded. Legend-only features (contact, drill-hole symbol) were not recorded as values. Two thicknesses printed with '|' for a digit are read as 1, flagged inferred and sent to review. The Toney Bay Member description begins 'The Waccamaw formation is ...' as printed. Low Falls beds have no description. Santee Limestone, Warley Hill formation and Lang Syne formation are listed as units in the cross section only.\nSUBSURFACE: cross section A-A' (page 1) is recorded with its vertical exaggeration and sea-level datum; its end labels are OCR'd as 'A |' and 'A!' (name inferred, sent to review), and its elevation scale (95 ft; 29 to 12 m), the Santee National Wildlife Refuge label and any unit labels can't be tied to distances, so no units or drill holes along it were recorded. Uppermost elevations of the Toney Bay Member (95 ft) and Marietta unit (135 ft) and the 80-ft river-terrace elevation are not tied to a place and stay in unit descriptions. A map-face label 'ELEVATION 77' could not be tied to a feature. Datum: horizontal 1927 North American Datum; contour interval 5 feet on the 1979 base map (page 1).",
